<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Reich Ministry for the Occupied Eastern Territories</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1941–1945</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Reich Ministry for the Occupied Eastern Territories was the Nazi German ministry created in July 1941 under Alfred Rosenberg to govern Soviet lands placed under civil administration. It oversaw the Reichskommissariats of Ostland and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a>, though the SS, the army and the commissioners often acted on their own. Its administration took part in the plunder, forced labour and mass murder carried out in these territories.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/reich-ministry-for-the-occupied-eastern-territories.jpg" alt="Reich Ministry for the Occupied Eastern Territories" width="320" height="209" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: RsVe. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Reichsadler_Deutsches_Reich_(1935%E2%80%931945).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
